###  http://w3id.org/mmvcomputedOn
<http://w3id.org/mmvcomputedOn> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                         <http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#DimensionProperty> .


###  http://w3id.org/mmvisMeasurementOf
<http://w3id.org/mmvisMeasurementOf> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                              <http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#DimensionProperty> .


###  http://w3id.org/mmvprecision
<http://w3id.org/mmvprecision> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                        <http://w3id.org/mmvDimension> ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Precision is a quality dimension, which refers to the recorded level of details. It represents the exactness of a measurement or description. It is equivalent the notion of Precision from ISO 25012."@en ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Precision"@en .


###  http://w3id.org/mmvqualityAssessment
<http://w3id.org/mmvqualityAssessment> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#Motivation> ;
                                       <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "Whenever DQV implementers need to extend the motivations for quality annotations, they should follow the instructions provided by the Web Annotation Data Model, and the concepts in the extension should be defined as specializations of dqv:qualityAssessment."@en ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#assessing> ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Motivation that must be specified for quality annotations."@en ;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Quality assessment"@en .


